        "It is not a ranking of the best books ever written, and it is not a sales chart. Plenty of great novels make ordinary audiobooks, and some titles earn their place mainly through the production, like Malcolm Gladwell's Talking to Strangers, built around archival tape, or the BBC's 1978 Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, which was a radio series before it was a novel. We passed over abridged editions where a complete one exists, and nothing released after mid-2025 is included, since listeners have not had time to settle on it.",
        "Use it as a menu. If you are new to audiobooks, start with the ten picks marked as starters, most of them under ten hours. Sections group recordings by kind (novels, genre fiction, memoir, history, full-cast drama and children's listening) and run in order of recording date within each. Lengths are for the edition named and can differ by a few minutes between retailers. Tick off what you have heard, save titles to your library under the book's name, and check each entry's notes for other recordings worth knowing.",
